 World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134937951,imgsize-730081.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chicago billionaire, 94, fed squirrels for years; now rats plague a park and market]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134937221.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-94-year-old-chicago-billionaire-hired-workers-to-scatter-nuts-around-lincoln-park-to-feed-squirrels-for-years-leftover-food-attracted-rats-damaged-park-property-and-disrupted-a-nearby-farmers-market/articleshow/134937221.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-94-year-old-chicago-billionaire-hired-workers-to-scatter-nuts-around-lincoln-park-to-feed-squirrels-for-years-leftover-food-attracted-rats-damaged-park-property-and-disrupted-a-nearby-farmers-market/articleshow/134937221.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T14:43:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134937571,imgsize-1768016.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[USDA-funded 2022 trial found cardboard garden beds had 15% weed cover, versus 45% in tilled beds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134936457.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Weeds can significantly impact crop yield, leading to a need for effective control methods. A USDA-funded trial demonstrated that cardboard beds reduced weed coverage compared to tilled beds. Farmers found that using cardboard made weeding easier and more efficient after two growing seasons. The results from the trial showed varied crop yields when grown in different bed types.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-2022-us-department-of-agriculture-funded-a-trial-by-spreading-cardboard-in-gardens-to-avoid-weeds-by-the-second-season-weeds-covered-only-15-of-the-cardboard-beds-compared-to-45-in-tilted-beds/articleshow/134936457.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-2022-us-department-of-agriculture-funded-a-trial-by-spreading-cardboard-in-gardens-to-avoid-weeds-by-the-second-season-weeds-covered-only-15-of-the-cardboard-beds-compared-to-45-in-tilted-beds/articleshow/134936457.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T14:14:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134936567,imgsize-1492160.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US judge allows CNN, MS NOW and Politico reporters to keep White House access]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134936891.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-judge-allows-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-reporters-to-keep-white-house-access-cites-first-amendment/articleshow/134936891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-judge-allows-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-reporters-to-keep-white-house-access-cites-first-amendment/articleshow/134936891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T14:04:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134937006,imgsize-37852.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bezos targets a sustainable lunar base after investing $28 billion since 2000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134935283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/were-going-to-the-moon-to-stay-jeff-bezos-targets-a-sustainable-lunar-base-after-investing-28-billion-in-blue-origin-since-2000/articleshow/134935283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/were-going-to-the-moon-to-stay-jeff-bezos-targets-a-sustainable-lunar-base-after-investing-28-billion-in-blue-origin-since-2000/articleshow/134935283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134935444,imgsize-698723.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Street Vendor Turns Concert Baklava Sales Into a $70,000-a-Month Business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134936142.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-street-vendor-turned-selling-baklava-outside-concerts-into-a-business-that-hit-nearly-70000-in-monthly-sales/articleshow/134936142.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-street-vendor-turned-selling-baklava-outside-concerts-into-a-business-that-hit-nearly-70000-in-monthly-sales/articleshow/134936142.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:16:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134936272,imgsize-174396.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[14-year-old wins Young Wildlife Photographer of the Year 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134935461.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[During a thrilling family game drive in Zimbabwe, Oscar Whitfield captured an extraordinary moment with a dung beetle, earning him the prestigious Young Grand Title at the 2026 Wildlife Photographer of the Year competition. Notable winners included Federico Veronesi, Amelie Davis, and James Lewin, each celebrated for their stunning depictions of wildlife. The captivating exhibition showcasing these masterpieces will commence at the Natural History Museum on Friday, 16 October 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/travel/news/oscar-whitfield-wins-2026-young-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-title-with-close-up-image-of-a-dung-beetle-in-zimbabwes-zambezi-national-park-along-with-five-other-stunning-pictures/articleshow/134935461.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/travel/news/oscar-whitfield-wins-2026-young-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-title-with-close-up-image-of-a-dung-beetle-in-zimbabwes-zambezi-national-park-along-with-five-other-stunning-pictures/articleshow/134935461.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:10:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134935948,imgsize-187743.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2020, Olivia Culpo launched More Than a Mask to fight pandemic hunger; her initiative went on to fund over 3 million meals through Feeding America]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134934167.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In May 2020, Olivia Culpo established More Than a Mask, an initiative aimed at combatting food insecurity worsened by the pandemic. By selling masks and collaborating with Feeding America, she provided meals to those in need. Culpo later partnered with Express to generate further donations for various charities, driven by her family's philanthropic spirit.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-olivia-culpo-launched-more-than-a-mask-to-fight-pandemic-hunger-her-initiative-went-on-to-fund-over-3-million-meals-through-feeding-america-according-to-her-2025-hall-of-fame-profile/articleshow/134934167.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-olivia-culpo-launched-more-than-a-mask-to-fight-pandemic-hunger-her-initiative-went-on-to-fund-over-3-million-meals-through-feeding-america-according-to-her-2025-hall-of-fame-profile/articleshow/134934167.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:06:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134934274,imgsize-733709.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ohio family stops Meta data center pipeline from crossing 40 acres of farmland]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134935141.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For over 60 years, the Luidhardt family has been dedicated to farming their land in Ohio, which was under threat from a proposed pipeline for Meta's data center. In a determined bid to protect their legacy, they challenged the route, leading to crucial legal discussions about how corporate interests impact family-run farms.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-family-farmed-the-same-land-for-at-least-three-generations-then-a-pipeline-linked-to-metas-data-center-was-mapped-across-40-acres-but-after-the-family-challenged-it-the-developer-chose-another-route/articleshow/134935141.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-family-farmed-the-same-land-for-at-least-three-generations-then-a-pipeline-linked-to-metas-data-center-was-mapped-across-40-acres-but-after-the-family-challenged-it-the-developer-chose-another-route/articleshow/134935141.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134935187,imgsize-84181.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[William Shatner’s kidney stone sold for $75,000, helping a Louisiana family get a home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134935616.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/william-shatner-underwent-kidney-stone-removal-the-stone-was-later-auctioned-for-75000-with-the-money-helping-a-louisiana-family-get-home/articleshow/134935616.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/william-shatner-underwent-kidney-stone-removal-the-stone-was-later-auctioned-for-75000-with-the-money-helping-a-louisiana-family-get-home/articleshow/134935616.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T12:56:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134935737,imgsize-1045714.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scarlett Johansson listed her 1931 Hollywood Hills villa for $4.95 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134934542.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scarlett Johansson has listed her stunning Spanish-style villa in the Hollywood Hills for $4.95 million. Acquired in 2007 for $7 million from director Harold Becker, this charming 1931-built property boasts four bedrooms and five and a half baths. The villa features modern renovations, including a stylish glass-topped atrium and a refreshing swimming pool, all while Johansson juggled her vibrant music career and her preparation for 'Iron Man 2.']]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/scarlett-johansson-listed-her-1931-hollywood-hills-villa-for-4-95-million-the-four-bedroom-home-had-gardens-terraces-and-a-pool/articleshow/134934542.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/scarlett-johansson-listed-her-1931-hollywood-hills-villa-for-4-95-million-the-four-bedroom-home-had-gardens-terraces-and-a-pool/articleshow/134934542.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134934814,imgsize-186568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Taylor Swift donates $1 million to a heart health organisation as US disease risk rises]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134910097.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Taylor Swift donated $1 million to the American Heart Association in 2025, honouring her father, Scott Swift, and his experience with heart disease. The contribution supports cardiovascular research, prevention programmes and access to care, as the organisation warns that rising disease rates could affect six in 10 Americans within 30 years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-swift-donates-1-million-to-heart-charity-in-honour-of-her-father-scott-swift-us-projections-warn-6-in-10-adults-could-have-cardiovascular-disease-by-2050s/articleshow/134910097.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-swift-donates-1-million-to-heart-charity-in-honour-of-her-father-scott-swift-us-projections-warn-6-in-10-adults-could-have-cardiovascular-disease-by-2050s/articleshow/134910097.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134910687,imgsize-830610.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists find volcanic lightning peaks 1.1 hours after first flash in major eruptions]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134934902.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/scientists-compared-lightning-from-16-major-eruptions-between-2010-and-2024-and-found-it-usually-peaked-0-5-to-2-hours-after-the-first-flash-averaging-1-1-hours-while-wider-ash-plumes-kept-it-going-longer/articleshow/134934902.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/scientists-compared-lightning-from-16-major-eruptions-between-2010-and-2024-and-found-it-usually-peaked-0-5-to-2-hours-after-the-first-flash-averaging-1-1-hours-while-wider-ash-plumes-kept-it-going-longer/articleshow/134934902.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134935032,imgsize-1124816.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Two Arizona brothers, aged 10 and 12, vanished into the desert; a helicopter-assisted search found them safe after eight hours]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134932805.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On October 11, a frantic search ensued for two young brothers, Atom and Jack Ward, who vanished while playing outside. Their worried father alerted authorities when they didn't return home. A collaborative effort involving local businesses and rescue teams, along with aerial support from the Arizona Department of Public Safety, led to their discovery six miles from home, with one boy still barefoot.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-arizona-brothers-aged-10-and-12-vanished-into-the-desert-trackers-followed-more-than-6-miles-of-footprints-before-a-helicopter-assisted-search-found-them-safe-after-eight-hours/articleshow/134932805.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-arizona-brothers-aged-10-and-12-vanished-into-the-desert-trackers-followed-more-than-6-miles-of-footprints-before-a-helicopter-assisted-search-found-them-safe-after-eight-hours/articleshow/134932805.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134932820,imgsize-1192730.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Polyethylene Microplastics And Liver Risk: Texas A&amp;M links exposure to fatty liver signs; questions remain for human health]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134933543.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New research from Texas A&amp;M University indicates that polyethylene microplastics may affect liver health negatively. The study observed significant signs of fatty liver disease linked to polyethylene exposure and a high-fat diet. Researchers found changes in gene activity related to fat metabolism and tissue repair. Future investigations will focus on whether these pollutants contribute to more severe liver damage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/researchers-found-that-polyethylene-microplastics-worsened-signs-of-fatty-liver-especially-when-combined-with-an-unhealthy-diet-raising-questions-about-a-plastic-used-in-everyday-packaging/articleshow/134933543.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/researchers-found-that-polyethylene-microplastics-worsened-signs-of-fatty-liver-especially-when-combined-with-an-unhealthy-diet-raising-questions-about-a-plastic-used-in-everyday-packaging/articleshow/134933543.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T12:01:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134933699,imgsize-1910318.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NASA’s Perseverance rover breaks Mars driving record, covering 28.1 miles in five years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134916000.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[NASA's Perseverance rover has set a new distance record on Mars, traveling 28.10 miles in its mission, eclipsing the previous record of 28.06 miles set by Opportunity in nearly 15 years. This remarkable feat, achieved over five and a half years, showcases Perseverance's advanced autonomous navigation system as it investigates ancient geological structures and collects rock samples to enhance our scientific insights.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/nasas-perseverance-rover-has-driven-farther-than-any-vehicle-on-another-world-after-five-and-a-half-years-on-mars-it-has-covered-28-10-miles-beating-opportunitys-15-year-record/articleshow/134916000.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/nasas-perseverance-rover-has-driven-farther-than-any-vehicle-on-another-world-after-five-and-a-half-years-on-mars-it-has-covered-28-10-miles-beating-opportunitys-15-year-record/articleshow/134916000.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T11:56:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134916181,imgsize-147394.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[11-year-old builds 450-member water network and moss filter to tackle lead in school water]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134933212.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nithya Tammana, a passionate young advocate, noticed rampant water wastage at home, prompting her to launch Save Drop. This initiative has attracted over 450 young changemakers dedicated to preserving water resources. Through impactful campaigns, she stresses the necessity of altering daily water conservation habits. Furthermore, she developed BioLayer, a nature-inspired water filter designed to enhance water quality, earning accolades for her contributions to environmental sustainability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/nithya-tammana-an-11-year-old-girl-from-new-jersey-built-a-youth-water-conservation-network-of-more-than-450-members-her-open-source-moss-filter-is-designed-to-remove-up-to-95-of-lead-from-school-drinking-water/articleshow/134933212.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/nithya-tammana-an-11-year-old-girl-from-new-jersey-built-a-youth-water-conservation-network-of-more-than-450-members-her-open-source-moss-filter-is-designed-to-remove-up-to-95-of-lead-from-school-drinking-water/articleshow/134933212.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T11:07:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134933419,imgsize-1452146.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Drew Barrymore sold her Hollywood Hills home in 2018; nearly 4 times its price]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134932230.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/n